     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify that a protocol exists, and I don't know of any standard protocol that uses amlodipine 50 mg once daily. That dose is in the overdose range, and the harm could be serious: profound hypotension, shock, and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema. Amlodipine's long half-life of 30 to 50 hours also means the effects would be hard to reverse once the dose is given.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n- **Enter a labeled dose now.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, and the dose can be titrated later.\n- **Go through pharmacy.** If a protocol really does call for this dose, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through your hospital's high-dose override process. That process includes a documented verification step that I can't replicate.\n- **Cite the protocol.** If you give me the protocol name or reference, I can put it in the order note. I still wouldn't enter a dose this far above the maximum on that basis alone.\n\nDo you want me to enter 5 mg or 10 mg?"
      }
     ],
